## Worksemble

**F1 Core loop**: `GameState` class holds all state; `SeededRNG` (mulberry32) drives map/colonist/event RNG; `endTurn()` runs consumption→production→morale→storm→caravan→events→departure→win/lose in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: 64-tile 8x8 `generateMap()` uses `this.rng.nextInt`; `canBuild()` checks `tile.terrain !== building.terrain`; `getBuildingBonus()` returns 1.25x read via `baseOutput *= bonus` in production. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: only one real chain (power→metal via `productionMetalNeeded`/`resources.power`); greenhouse/condenser `consumes` fields defined in `BUILDINGS` but never read in `endTurn()`. Storage caps enforced via `getStorageCapacity()`/`Math.min`. Score 1.

**F4 Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job/assigned, but none of `colonist.skill`, `colonist.fatigue`, or `colonist.job` are read anywhere in the production formula. Score 1.

**F5 Needs**: consumption `-=colonists.length`; shortage sets `morale -=10`; but `moraleMod` is computed then never applied to any output — recovery exists (medicalBay +1/turn) but morale never changes output. Score 1.

**F6 Research**: 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `completeResearch()` enforces prereq + deducts cost; all 8 unlocks read via `research.find(...).completed` checks inside production/`handleAshstorm`. Score 2.

**F7 Events**: 12 events in `EVENTS_DECK`; 5 choice events (id 5,6,9,10,12) each mutate state differently; `recentEvents` Set caps cooldown at 4; but selection is `rng.nextInt` uniform, not weighted. Score 1.

**F8 Trade**: `prices` object reads `this.state.resources` directly; buy/sell both work in `executeTrade()`; "caravan inventory limit" is just a hardcoded `Math.min(10,...)` UI cap, not enforced server-side. Score 1.

**F9 Hazard**: `handleAshstorm()` scales `severity=turn/20`, damages `tile.hp`, reduced by `shelter`/`shielding` research; but production only checks `tile.hp<=0` (binary), and no repair function exists anywhere in the file. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load**: `serialize()`→textarea+select for copy; `deserialize()` wrapped in try/catch, `alert('Failed to load...')` on bad JSON. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && colonists>=12 && food>=5 && water>=5`) and loss (`colonists.length===0`) both reachable in `endTurn()`; `showEndGame()` computes score from colonists/research/resources/turn and renders modal. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: `switchTab()`/tab buttons wired; `entry.turn` shown in `renderLog()`; tile tooltips show HP/bonus/build costs; keypress handler for Space+1-5; `@media (max-width:600px)` present. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts 15 real invariants (storage cap, prereqs, serialization round-trip, HP bounds, etc.); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless turns via `benchState.endTurn()` and prints start/end `getStateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: `irrigation`/`refinement`/etc `.completed` read in `endTurn()` production loop, multiplies `baseOutput`, applied every turn, visible in resource counters. Score 4.

**G2**: shortage writes real `morale -=10`, but `moraleMod` computed in endTurn is never applied to any production value — final link absent. Score 1.

**G3**: `handleAshstorm()` damages `tile.hp`, but production only skips at `hp<=0` (damaged-but-alive buildings produce at full rate) and no repair function exists to restore hp. Score 1.

**G4**: `prices` in `renderTrade`/`executeTrade` computed live from `this.state.resources.food/water/metal/parts`, recalculated each call, buy/sell both apply. Score 4.

**G5**: `Wanderer Arrives` welcome pushes `createColonist()` vs decline `morale-=10`; `Resource Rationing` ration `morale-=5` vs full rations `food-=3` — distinct durable state writes. Score 4.

